Tom

Thank you for Monday's call. I spoke to the board last night and we have decided.

Zeevonk's bank has told them it will not release the deposit for the Curlew Bay while Kingsholm are threatening to arrest her. We cannot let the sale slip, and the buyers' timetable is tight. So we will pay Kingsholm the USD 184,500.00 they are claiming on Friday 9 October. We will pay it under protest and without admitting that it is due. Gareth will make the transfer that morning.

I would be grateful if you would:

1. Tell Imogen Pryce at Dunmere Pryce today that we are paying under protest and without admission, and that the payment does not settle the dispute.
2. Claim back the USD 88,200.00 we will have overpaid. As your letter of 23 September said, we still say demurrage is USD 96,300.00.

This replaces the settlement authority we discussed. I do not want to negotiate with Kingsholm any further on the price; I want the difference back.

Please call me on 01632 960150 if you want to talk before Friday.

